WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[Music and applause]

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Coraline Jones always dreamed of finding a world

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:19.000
[Music]

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:27.000
better, a world more exciting than this one, but she never imagined she would

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:37.000
discover it in her own home.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:46.000
A parallel place...
—We've been waiting for you, Coraline.
—...where parents are always fun.
—I love your garden. This is

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:55.000
amazing.
—And everything is so perfect...
—Come in, dear.
—...that it can't be

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:01.000
real.
—Right on time, dinner is ready.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.000
[Applause]

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:09.000
—She has buttons, do you like them? I'm your other mother, silly. Can you believe this world

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:16.000
is a dream come true?
—My name?
—Don't you like it here?
—No, Coraline.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:24.000
—You could stay forever. There's just one tiny thing we need to do.
—You're welcome, black is

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:32.000
traditional.
She lives in a world where everything is better, but it's a trap.
—You can leave when you learn to be a good

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:42.000
daughter.
Henry Selick, the director of The Nightmare Before Christmas, brings us a world of extraordinary

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:49.000
imagination, spine-tingling secrets...
—Who are you?
—You're in grave

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:57.000
danger.
—...and daring discoveries.
—I have to find my parents and set them free.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:03.000
When adventure calls, there are

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:13.000
doors that must never be opened.
—I'm not

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:19.000
afraid.
Coraline. Written and directed by Henry Selick.

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:23.000
[Music]